    "reading": {
        "body": "CoreWeave's quarterly capital expenditure reached 7.7 billion dollars in the quarter ending March 2026, more than five times the 1.4 billion dollars it reported one year earlier, the sharpest single-year jump of any builder in this peer set.\n\nThe series covers three March quarters a year apart, 1.74 billion in 2024, a decline to 1.41 billion in 2025, then a jump to 7.7 billion in 2026. That pattern, a dip followed by a sudden multiple-fold increase, makes CoreWeave the most volatile capex trajectory among the eight builders tracked here, in contrast to the steadier upward climbs reported by Amazon and Equinix over the same period.\n\nCoreWeave filed six separate SEC disclosures in 2026 alone, in March, April twice, May, June, and August, each recording new financial obligations or related agreements, far more filing activity than any other builder in this set, where Amazon and Alphabet each filed twice and Microsoft and Digital Realty filed none. That filing pace matches the scale of the spending increase, and together they describe a company financing a rapid buildout through a continuous sequence of individual agreements rather than the fewer, larger transactions seen at Equinix or Amazon. CoreWeave's 7.7 billion dollars now sits just below Oracle's 8.5 billion, making it the fifth largest capex figure in this peer group despite having reported a fraction of that spending as recently as 2025.",
